        "description": "Exploit the known structure of good 14-point solutions: the optimal configuration likely has dmax realized by few antipodal-like pairs. Parametrize the configuration as 7 near-antipodal pairs (points \u00b1vi plus small radial perturbations), reducing dimensionality. Then maximize the minimum of the 91 distances using a smooth exact reformulation: minimize sum of exp(-d^2/temperature) via scipy.optimize.minimize (method='L-BFGS-B' or 'trust-constr') over the ~21 pair-direction parameters plus per-point radii. This drastically reduces the search space and directly encodes that dmax is a diameter. Multiple random initial pair directions (e.g., from icosahedron axes, Thomson-like solutions) give diverse basins.",
